ings**\n   - **Node Overlap Prevention**: Simple Fibonacci sphere distribution caused overlaps when projected; combining an electrostatic repulsion pass with golden-angle 2D spiral offset in sub-networks completely eliminates overlaps.\n   - **Dynamic Morphing Requirement**: Node sizes in both 3D and 2D sub-networks depend on active degree ($Size = \\max(9, 8 + 2.2 \\sqrt{Degree})$). When sub-network layers are toggled, active degrees must recalculate and sizes morph dynamically.\n   - **No Icons Constraint**: User strictly prohibited vector/flat icons or emojis in node frames and layout buttons. Replaced with SVG stroke geometry for header buttons and photo thumbnails/monospace badges for nodes.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - Single standalone HTML file: `hyperbolic_3d_network.html` with native HTML5 Canvas and vanilla JS (no external libraries).\n   - Local URI: `file:///C:/Users/aleja/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d3de736b-bad3-4cd4-b3f7-8b59f3dfee52/hyperbolic_3d_network.html`.\n\n5. **Next Steps**\n   - Update `renderSubNetworkCanvas()` and `toggleSubCat()` so that when sub-network category layers are toggled or nodes are hidden, sub-network node degrees are dynamically recalculated and node sizes morph reactively (matching the main 3D graph behavior).\n   - Perform runtime verification to confirm smooth size morphing and edge re-linking in the Sub-Network 2D view.\n   - Summarize the final result to the user.\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - **No Emojis / No Flat Icons inside nodes**: Use real species photos or monospace ID text badges only.\n   - **No Linear / Cross Layouts**: Sub-network must remain an organic web.\n   - **Camera Freeze**: Rotation must freeze while modal/inspector is active.\n   - **Dynamic Size Morphing**: Toggling sub-network layer buttons must recalculate degree and morph node sizes in real time.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 6 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1791155527029]\nPath: file:///C: